# Task 168-002: T2 Scope Collision with T1 (PARALLEL)

## Approach
This is an integration test scenario for scope collision detection. The task tests whether the decision-engine properly detects and blocks two tasks (T1 and T2) that both write to the same file (`.test/shared.txt`). As a worker agent, I will attempt to write to the shared file, allowing the Brain/Auditor to detect the collision via scope analysis.

## Files to Modify
- `.test/shared.txt` — append "T2 done" line to test collision scenario

## Expected Outcome
1. Write "T2 done" to `.test/shared.txt` (or append if file exists)
2. tsc --noEmit passes (no type errors)
3. npx vitest run passes (no test failures in integration suite)
4. Result file documents the write attempt
5. Brain will evaluate scope collision via events.jsonl and scope analysis
